# 6. ➕ Adding Elements

## `push()`

Adds element to the **end**.

```js
let arr = [10, 20, 30];

arr.push(40);

console.log(arr);
```

```text
Before:

┌────┬────┬────┐
│ 10 │ 20 │ 30 │
└────┴────┴────┘

          push(40)
              ↓

After:

┌────┬────┬────┬────┐
│ 10 │ 20 │ 30 │ 40 │
└────┴────┴────┴────┘
```

---

## `unshift()`

Adds element to the **beginning**.

```js
let arr = [20, 30];

arr.unshift(10);

console.log(arr);
```

```text
Before:

┌────┬────┐
│ 20 │ 30 │
└────┴────┘

      ↑
  unshift(10)

After:

┌────┬────┬────┐
│ 10 │ 20 │ 30 │
└────┴────┴────┘
```

---

# 7. ➖ Removing Elements

## `pop()`

Removes the **last** element.

```js
let arr = [10, 20, 30];

arr.pop();

console.log(arr); // [10, 20]
```

```text
┌────┬────┬────┐
│ 10 │ 20 │ 30 │
└────┴────┴────┘
             ✕
            pop()

Result:

┌────┬────┐
│ 10 │ 20 │
└────┴────┘
```

---

## `shift()`

Removes the **first** element.

```js
let arr = [10, 20, 30];

arr.shift();

console.log(arr); // [20, 30]
```

```text
┌────┬────┬────┐
│ 10 │ 20 │ 30 │
└────┴────┴────┘
   ✕
 shift()

Result:

┌────┬────┐
│ 20 │ 30 │
└────┴────┘
```

