# 18. 🆚 Array Reference Behavior

Arrays are objects in JavaScript.

```js
let a = [10, 20, 30];

let b = a;

b.push(40);

console.log(a);
```

Output:

```text
[10, 20, 30, 40]
```

Why?

```text
             STACK                 HEAP

          ┌─────────┐
          │ a ──────┼──────────┐
          ├─────────┤          │
          │ b ──────┼──────┐   │
          └─────────┘      │   │
                           │   ↓
                           │ ┌──────────────┐
                           └→│ 10 20 30 40  │
                             └──────────────┘
```

Both `a` and `b` point to the **same array**.

