# 🎯 Must Remember

```text
1. Array index starts at 0.

2. Last index = length - 1.

3. Arrays are objects in JavaScript.

4. Arrays are mutable.

5. push()     → add at end
6. pop()      → remove from end
7. unshift()  → add at beginning
8. shift()    → remove from beginning

9. map()      → transform → new array
10. filter()  → select → new array
11. reduce()  → many values → one result
12. forEach() → execute for each element

13. splice()  → add/remove/replace → mutates
14. slice()   → extract/copy → does not mutate

15. b = a     → same array reference
16. b = [...a] → shallow copy
```

## 🧠 Ultimate Memory Trick

```text
PUSH    → Put at the end
POP     → Pull from the end

UNSHIFT → Put at the beginning
SHIFT   → Pull from the beginning

MAP     → Modify/transform every item
FILTER  → Find/select matching items
REDUCE  → Reduce many → one
FOREACH → Do something for each

SPLICE  → Change the original
SLICE   → Take a portion without changing original
```
